"""Where PAC's missions come from.

Each scenario is a kind of real air-cargo work: who ships what, from where to where, and when in the year it happens.
The mission board draws from these to keep a living board: a couple of weeks of work at any time, different every
few days, with seasonal work appearing in its season. Airports are real ICAO codes; any that aren't in PAC's airport
data, or can't be reached by the fleet, are simply skipped.

max_lbs caps the load where real shipments are small (isotopes, art, AOG parts), whatever the aircraft.
Placeholders in titles and briefings: {o} {d} origin/destination ICAO, {oc} {dc} cities, {cargo} ({Cargo} capitalised),
{month}, and {challenge}: what makes the airport hard (CHALLENGES).

Optional scenario fields: "ferry" (no cargo, pays the ferry bonus), "types" (only these aircraft), "challenge" (the
airport note goes into the briefing and the dossier) and "handling" (special-cargo handling notes for the dossier).
"""

